The commit introduces the call to `amd_pstate_set_epp()` and its error handling in `amd_pstate_epp_cpu_init()`. Specifically, lines 1530-1533 show: 

+   ret = amd_pstate_set_epp(cpudata, cpudata->epp_default);
+   if (ret)
+           return ret;

This returns the error code directly instead of jumping to a cleanup label to free the allocated `cpudata` object, which is the exact root cause of the vulnerability.
